          "Culture": "en",
          "Value": "For different types of documents, the context can have a different type and have its own set of properties.\nTo use these properties, you first need to bring the context to the specified type. This can be done explicitly or via the As<TType>() helper method.\n\nThe following context types are possible:\n* StringPlaceholderReplaceExtensionContext - context of text document extensions.\n* WordPlaceholderReplaceExtensionContext - context of Word document extensions.\n* ExcelPlaceholderReplaceExtensionContext - context of Excel document extensions."
